# Kemono Downloader Release Notes

## Unreleased
**fix: crash-proof error handling, Tor that never falls back to a direct connection, Pawchive previews, Linux packaging, translations, docs and CI**

- Explain files the site only has previews of, instead of failing on them.
  Pawchive lists many files whose full copy is gone and only the thumbnail remains; downloading them failed with "404 Client Error" and was retried up to 50 times each, which looked like a broken app (one creator had over 8,000 such files). The site marks these files, so the downloaders now skip them, log one line per batch, and show a warning window (it doesn't pause the downloads) that explains why and lists the files, with a pointer to the Thumbnail Downloader tab for saving the previews. The Post tab shows them as "preview only" and they can't be selected. A file the media server doesn't have (HTTP 404 or 410) is no longer retried on any site and is reported in plain words, and each download ends with a summary of how many files were downloaded, only previews, not on the server, or failed. Progress counts no longer include the skipped files.

- Save previews, show missing files, and use fewer requests.
  A new setting, "Save the preview image when the site only has a preview of a file" (off by default), saves the preview of such images instead, named like `00501_preview.png`. At the end of a download, a window lists any files the media server didn't have, on every site. The History tab's files column explains how many files were only previews or missing, and the CSV export includes both counts. Pawchive files are requested straight from the server the site names, one request less per file, falling back to the usual address if that server fails; already-downloaded files are still recognised. The Post tab's file-type filters now apply while files are prepared (they were read incorrectly and only applied later), and the in-app Help gives the right download range (1-20, default 5) and explains preview-only and missing files.

- Retry incomplete downloads in the Creator tab.
  When a file arrived shorter than the server announced (usually a dropped connection), the Creator tab deleted it and gave up after one attempt, although its retry setting allowed more; the Post tab already retried. Both tabs now treat it as a network error and retry it.

- Keep the app running after an unexpected error.
  An error that nothing else caught used to make PyQt abort the whole app without a message (on Windows, exit code 0xC0000409). The app now prints the error, shows a dialog with the details to include in a bug report, and keeps running.

- Never bypass Tor when it is selected.
  With Tor chosen as the proxy but not running, downloads used to go straight to the site without any proxy, and a missing PySocks package switched to a Privoxy port the app never starts. Requests now always go to Tor's SOCKS port and fail if Tor isn't available, so the real IP address is never used by accident. This also works with a Tor service you run yourself on the default port. Proxy settings are no longer printed to the console on every request.

- Update the built-in Tor download to 16.0.1 and verify it.
  "Download Tor" now fetches the Tor 16.0.1 Expert Bundle, checks it against the SHA-256 published in Tor's signed checksum list before extracting anything, and refuses a file that doesn't match. Linux on ARM64 gets the matching bundle, and an unsupported system shows a message instead of downloading a bundle that can't run.

- Translate the remaining English-only interface text.
  The Tor status while starting, the Tor Help button and help dialog, the "Custom Proxy" option, folder errors in Settings, the Post tab's log saving messages, the Creator tab's log messages and Expand Logs tooltip, and the Thumbnail tab's preview hint now follow the selected language. Changing the language while Tor runs no longer shows it as stopped. Twenty unused translations were removed.

- Use one "JPG/JPEG" file-type option in the Post tab, as in the Creator tab; both extensions were already filtered together.

- Correct the documentation.
  The simultaneous downloads range is 1-20 (the docs and the in-app Help said 1-10, and the Help gave the default as 10 instead of 5), and the README's retry limits now match the app. The security policy covers the latest release, explains that GitHub issues are public, and offers private GitHub vulnerability reports; the Code of Conduct and Support page no longer suggest "private issues". The pull request template names the current sites, and the contributing guide explains how to run the tests and checks.

- Trim dependencies and update the build configuration.
  Pillow is no longer installed: the app never used it. `requirements.txt` names `beautifulsoup4` like the packaging config. Flatpak builds use the KDE 6.11 runtime and the matching PyQt base app instead of 6.7.

- Test every supported Python in CI.
  Tests now run on Python 3.9 to 3.14 (3.9, 3.11 and 3.14 on Windows, macOS and Linux; 3.10, 3.12 and 3.13 on Linux), where they ran on 3.9 to 3.11 only. The code checks run once in their own job instead of in every test job, and pyright is pinned so a new release can't fail CI on unchanged code.

- Fix the website's build steps and links.
  The page replaced several sections with translations that had lost their markup, so the build steps showed no commands, and the Support, Contributing and License links disappeared, in English, Japanese and Korean. The steps now match the README (virtual environment, Linux libraries, `briefcase dev`), the dependency list is complete, and documentation links open the rendered pages on GitHub.

- Fix crashes when creator background tasks finish.
  The Creator tab's URL validation, post detection, file preparation, filtering and check-all threads could be destroyed while they were still finishing, and Qt then aborted the whole app ("QThread: Destroyed while thread is still running"). Their cleanup now waits for each thread to exit first.

- Fix Pawchive file previews.
  Previews in the Post and Creator tabs now send the same identifiable user agent as downloads; Pawchive's file server refuses browser user agents with HTTP 403. The Pawchive request policy (user agent, pacing and the five-download cap) now also applies to every `pawchive.<suffix>` domain instead of only `pawchive.pw`.

- Accept Pawchive post URLs by the site's own name.
  Post URL validation no longer depends on a Pawchive page mentioning Kemono or Coomer.

- Fix the built-in Tor setup.
  On Linux it could configure the bundle's debug symbols (`debug/tor`) as the Tor program, which cannot run; it now uses `tor/tor`. The Tor download has a timeout instead of waiting forever on a stalled connection, links in the archive that point outside the Tor folder are refused, and a failed download no longer leaves its partial archive in the temp folder.

- Declare the system libraries Qt needs on Linux.
  The `.deb`, `.rpm`, openSUSE and Arch packages now depend on the X11 libraries the Qt platform plugin loads, including `xcb-cursor`, whose absence made the app abort at launch with "Could not load the Qt platform plugin xcb". The package description was shortened to Briefcase's recommended length and now mentions Pawchive.

- Update the documentation.
  The READMEs explain how to install `xcb-cursor` on Linux and now say correctly where builds are available (pre-compiled binaries on Ko-fi; the GitHub Releases page has release notes and source code). The website mentions Pawchive and has the five Simplified Chinese strings it was missing (its language button showed "undefined").

- Improve CI.
  Tests run on the new Ubuntu 26.04 runners (Python 3.9 stays on Ubuntu 24.04, which still has it), one failing job no longer cancels the others, GitHub Actions are updated to their Node 24 versions, pip downloads are cached, the workflow can be run manually, superseded pull request runs are cancelled, and only test reports are uploaded.

- Make the test suite more reliable.
  Thread tests wait for their threads to stop before returning (an intermittent abort in CI), tests no longer write a history database into the repository or `/tmp`, and new tests cover the Pawchive request policy, the Tor download and the version numbers.

## v5.14.0 (03 November 2026)
**feat: History tab with download history and favorites, a smoother and faster interface, and download reliability fixes**

- Add a History tab (`kd_history.py`, `history_store.py`).
  Every finished or cancelled post, creator and thumbnail download is recorded with its links, files (done/total and failures), posts, size on disk, duration, status and folder. Search, filter by type, sort any column, and see totals for what is shown. Open a download's folder, or recover when it was moved, renamed or deleted (locate it, open the nearest parent folder, or download it again). Copy links, send them back to the right downloader queue, save them to favorites, remove entries or clear the history (downloaded files are never touched), export the list as CSV, or pause recording.

- Add Favorites.
  Save post and creator links with the new star button in the Post and Creator tabs, from the history, or by pasting a link. Edit titles and notes, see when each favorite was last downloaded, queue it in one click, open it in the browser, and import or export favorites as a `.txt` list. History and favorites are stored in `library.db` beside the hash database; an unreadable file is set aside and recreated, and an unwritable folder falls back to an in-memory store with a warning.

- Make launching instant and the interface smoother.
  The tabs are built in the background while the intro screen is showing, so clicking Launch responds in milliseconds instead of blocking for about a second. The intro now fades in, Launch crossfades into the main screen, and switching tabs by click crossfades between pages (the previous window-opacity fades never displayed). Mouse-wheel scrolling glides, lists scroll by pixel, and the file and overall progress bars ease to new values. The Help manual is rendered as one document (about 430 ms faster to build) and its links are clickable.

- Start faster and stop waiting on the network at startup.
  The supported-domain list is read from the bundled file and refreshed in the background, so the app no longer blocks on it (startup without a network connection: about 6 s to 1 s).

- Make downloads lighter on the interface and memory.
  Progress is reported at most once per percentage point and files stream in 64 KB chunks (a 200 MB file sends about 101 progress updates instead of 25,600). Files are hashed while they download and existing files are verified in 1 MB blocks, off the creator downloader's event loop (peak memory for a 200 MB file: about 210 MB to 12 MB). The full logs window shares the console's document instead of re-rendering a copy every half second, and large debug dumps are shortened. The creator downloader's worker pool now honours the "simultaneous downloads" setting above the CPU count.

- Fix downloads reported finished too early.
  The post downloader stopped waiting for its workers after 30 seconds, so large files could be marked complete while still downloading, and file preparation could silently drop files. Workers are now awaited for as long as a download runs, with a grace period only after cancelling.

- Fix several download and interface bugs.
  - Server-supplied file names can no longer escape the download folder (for example `..\..\file.exe`), and characters Windows rejects are replaced.
  - Partial files are removed when a download finally fails.
  - Compressed responses no longer fail with a false size mismatch.
  - Missing request timeouts were added, so a stalled server can no longer hang a download thread.
  - Cancelling stops retry and back-off loops promptly instead of letting threads sleep through their remaining retries.
  - Creator post search no longer drops text typed while a search is running.
  - Creator post rows were built twice; they are now built once.
  - The Post tab no longer shows stray numbers such as "0 0 0 0" after progress labels.
  - Log lines escape titles and file names instead of rendering them as markup.
  - The idle status label updates in every language, including Simplified Chinese.
  - Six translation keys the app already used were missing, so some dialog titles showed raw names such as "warning"; they are now translated in all four languages.

- Fix native crashes.
  Closing the app no longer crashes on exit, clicking Launch during the intro fade no longer crashes, and scrolling over a tab no longer crashes. The History tab destroys its tables before their data models.

- Refactor shared code into `download_utils.py`, `kd_network.py`, `kd_logs.py` and `kd_motion.py`.
  Removes code that was duplicated between the downloaders (about 560 fewer lines) and the dependency of the Post Downloader on the Creator Downloader module.

- Remove the unused `aiohttp` and `asyncio` requirements.

- Make the test suite reliable and offline.
  Tests can no longer reach the internet, a test that started a real network thread was fixed, and leaked test threads are stopped cooperatively before any forced termination; together these fix an intermittent access-violation crash in full test runs. Adds tests for the history store and tab, the recording hooks, translation coverage in every language, the motion helpers, and the download fixes.

## v5.13.0 (27 September 2026)
**fix: responsible Pawchive request pacing and improved resilience to HTTP 403 responses**

- Add a Pawchive-specific identifiable user agent with a contact address instead of impersonating a browser.
- Limit Pawchive file downloads to five active downloads across the Post and Creator Downloaders, while continuing to respect the user's lower simultaneous-download setting.
- Pace new Pawchive file requests to at most one per second, including retry attempts, to reduce server overload and help prevent transient HTTP 403 responses.
- Add a Settings info button explaining the Pawchive policy and update the ethical-use documentation.

## v5.12.0 (01 August 2026)
**feat: Thumbnail Downloader tab, Auto Rename by order, and Post Text description downloading**

- Add new Thumbnail Downloader tab (`kd_thumbnaildl.py`).
  Introduces a dynamic thumbnail-only downloader tab supporting both Post Mode and Creator Mode. Features URL queue management, bulk file import, filter search, multi-selection, preview modal integration, and UI locking during detection and download operations.

- Mirror creator folder strategy settings for thumbnail downloads.
  Thumbnails follow the exact folder layout configured in settings (`per_post`, `by_file_type`, or `single_folder`) under `Downloads/Thumbnails/{user_id}_{creator_name}/`.

- Add "Auto Rename and sort File name by order" option for thumbnails.
  Optionally prepends per-post sequential ordering indexes (`1_`, `2_`, `3_`...) to downloaded thumbnail filenames for easy sorting.

- Add "Download Post Text" description option for thumbnails.
  Optionally fetches and saves post descriptions (`desc_{post_id}.txt`) alongside thumbnails with automatic HTML stripping via BeautifulSoup and 403 HTTP bypass handling (`Accept: text/css`).

- Dynamic domain context propagation and robust API error handling.
  Ensures service API calls, creator profile metadata resolution, and post text extraction correctly target the originating domain (`kemono.cr`, `coomer.st`, etc.) with 403 Cloudflare bypass retries.

- Unit tests and integration test suite expansion.
  Adds 11 comprehensive unit tests covering thumbnail detection, download thread, folder strategies, hash DB integration, preview modal, UI filter controls, and post text file creation.

## v5.11.1 (05 July 2026)
**fix: dynamic pawchive domain suffix resolution and documentation refresh**

- Replace hardcoded `pawchive.st` handling with dynamic `pawchive.<suffix>` support.
  The downloader now derives the active pawchive suffix from the domain list configuration and builds file hosts dynamically (`file.pawchive.<suffix>`), avoiding breakage when pawchive domains rotate.

- Improve pawchive file URL normalization for dynamic domains.
  URL cleanup now rewrites direct pawchive links to the correct file host based on the active suffix and still enforces `/data/` path normalization for compatibility.

- Update tests and release documentation for v5.11.1.
  Refreshed pawchive URL tests to be suffix-agnostic and updated version metadata/docs for this patch release.

## v5.11.0 (17 June 2026)
**feat: dynamic domain configuration and pawchive.st support**

- Add dynamic domain configuration and pawchive.st support
  Introduces a new `assets/config/domain` file to centralize domain names (kemono.cr, coomer.st, pawchive.st). The application now dynamically loads these domains, improving maintainability and allowing for easier updates to supported sites.

- Update license definitions to use PEP 639 format
  Refactored `pyproject.toml` to comply with PEP 639 for license metadata, ensuring better compatibility with modern Python packaging standards.

- Improve download reliability and system compatibility
  - Introduce `XDG_DATA_HOME` fallback on Linux for reliable data storage.
  - Improve download interruption handling: partial files are now removed only after the file handle is closed, preventing potential crashes and ensuring cleaner state recovery.
  - Removal of failed/interrupted files now gracefully handles `OSError`.

- Comprehensive test suite expansion and CI stability improvements
  - Mock `QMediaPlayer` and `QAudioOutput` to prevent native multimedia backend crashes in headless CI.
  - Add an autouse fixture to reliably clean up leaked `QThreads` after each test.
  - Add over 100 new unit tests covering `Creator Downloader`, fast-mode UI flows, file/download edge cases, preview caching, and post detection threads (including gzipped responses).
  - Silenced `urllib3` OpenSSL/LibreSSL warnings in `pytest` configuration.

## v5.10.0 (10 February 2026)
**feat: Fast Mode, SQLite hash storage, and customizable font settings**

- Add file size validation to HashDB for corruption detection
  Adds a `file_size` column to the SQLite hash database schema. When a file is successfully downloaded, its actual size on disk is now stored alongside the hash. On subsequent download attempts, the stored file size is compared against the existing file's size before performing the more expensive MD5 hash check. If a size mismatch is detected (indicating corruption or incomplete download), the file is automatically re-downloaded. Includes automatic schema migration for existing databases (ALTER TABLE) and backward compatibility for legacy JSON-migrated entries (default file_size of 0). Adds 7 new unit tests covering file_size storage, retrieval, corruption detection, legacy migration, and old-DB schema migration.

- Fix progress bars to accurately reflect download progress
  Resolves multiple issues causing progress bars to not reflect actual download state:
  - **Post Downloader**: Added `bool` success flag to `file_completed` signal (now `pyqtSignal(int, str, bool)`), matching Creator Downloader's existing pattern. Failed files now emit `file_completed(index, url, False)` instead of silently returning, ensuring they are counted in progress.
  - **Post Downloader**: Removed premature `file_completed` emission from inside the chunk download loop (was firing at progress == 100 before size validation completed).
  - **Both Downloaders**: Overall progress bar now calculates percentage as `(completed + failed) / total` instead of `completed / total`, so failed files no longer stall the progress bar.
  - **Post Downloader**: Added `failed_files` tracking set to the UI class with proper clearing alongside `completed_files` at all reset points.
  - **Post Downloader**: Download completion check now uses `completed + failed >= total` instead of `completed == total`.

- Add Fast Mode to Post Downloader and Creator Downloader
  Introduces a Fast Mode toggle (with qtawesome bolt icon) to both downloader tabs. When enabled, Fast Mode automatically selects all download categories, locks manual options to prevent accidental changes, and reveals a batch URL input area for pasting multiple URLs at once (one per line). Completed items are automatically removed from the queue. An info button (ℹ) explains the feature in a dialog. Includes full translations for all four languages and new unit tests.

- Fix Creator Downloader fast mode batch download
  In fast mode, pressing Download now auto-detects and downloads all posts for each queued creator sequentially instead of requiring manual post selection. Uses a pipeline of `_fast_mode_process_next()` → PostDetectionThread → `_fast_mode_auto_download()` → `prepare_files_for_download()` to process each creator URL and advance to the next on completion.

- Lock UI controls during active downloads
  All UI elements (inputs, checkboxes, buttons, queue lists, pagination, other tabs, and settings tab) are disabled during a download in both Post and Creator downloader tabs. Only the Cancel button and Expand Logs remain enabled. New `set_downloading_ui_state()` method in both tabs provides comprehensive lock/unlock behavior.

- Fix Expand Logs window freezing
  Both Post and Creator downloader LogsWindow dialogs now use QTimer-based batched updates (500ms interval) instead of synchronous HTML copying on every log entry, preventing UI freezes during heavy download logging.

- Migrate file deduplication from JSON to SQLite
  Replaces the `file_hashes.json` flat-file backend with a new `hash_db.py` module backed by SQLite (WAL mode, thread-safe). The `HashDB` class provides `has()`, `add()`, `remove()`, and `all_hashes()` methods. Existing JSON hash files are automatically migrated on first access. Improves performance and reliability for large hash sets. Includes 16 unit tests covering CRUD, migration, and thread safety.

- Add font settings to the Settings tab
  Introduces a new Font Settings group in the settings UI, allowing users to switch the application-wide font between JetBrains Mono (default) and Poppins. Fonts are bundled as TTF files (Regular, Bold, Medium weights) and loaded at startup via QFontDatabase. The selected font is persisted via QSettings and applied across the entire application, including the intro screen, help tab, and browser extension tab. Adds `font_changed` signal to SettingsTab, dynamic `_get_font_family()` helpers in HelpTab and ExtensionTab, recursive font propagation in `KemonoDownloader.apply_font()`, and translations for the font UI in all four languages (English, Japanese, Korean, Chinese-Simplified). Includes 39 new unit tests covering defaults, combo box, signal emission, dialog messages, reset, bundled files, translations, QSettings persistence, and UI elements.

- **fix:** Replace `locale.getlocale(locale.LC_ALL)` with `locale.getlocale(locale.LC_CTYPE)` in downloader modules to prevent `TypeError` on Python 3.14/CachyOS; ensures locale detection works across all OSes and Python versions.

- Include PyQt BaseApp in Flatpak config to provide `libgssapi_krb5.so.2` and prevent runtime crashes


## v5.9.0 (09 February 2026)
**feat: Creator filename/folder customization, browser extension, and misc fixes**
- Add creator filename/folder customization
  Introduce customizable filename templates and folder strategies for the Creator downloader. Added SettingsTab options and persistence for `creator_filename_template` and `creator_folder_strategy`, UI widgets (preset templates, editable custom template, help button, folder strategy combo) and translated labels in `kd_language`. Implemented `generate_filename_and_folder` and `get_desc_folder_for_post` in `CreatorDownloadThread` to build sanitized filenames and target folders (`per_post` / `single_folder` / `by_file_type`), support auto-rename counters, avoid duplicating creator folder segments, and write per-post description files (`desc_{post_id}.txt`) into appropriate folders. Added top-level exception protection and logging in download threads for more robust error handling. Added faulthandler enable in `tests/conftest.py` and multiple unit tests covering templates, folder strategies, UI behavior, and thread safety. Also updated `.gitignore` (add `.briefcase`) and extended settings confirmation/applied dialogs to include the new options.

- Add initial Kemono Downloader browser extension
  Introduce a standalone browser extension for downloading content from Kemono and Coomer sites. Includes background script for downloads and CORS handling, content script for UI and post parsing, manifest, assets, and documentation.

- Add browser extension tab and documentation
  Introduces a new 'Browser Extension' tab in the application, providing users with information and instructions for the standalone browser extension. Updates the README with a detailed section on the browser extension, and adds relevant translations and UI logic to support the new tab.

- Improve file progress display and direct downloads of the browser extension
  Enhanced progress messages in the background script to include file index and total, improving clarity during multi-file downloads. Added filename truncation for better UI in content script, and switched to direct anchor-based downloads for ZIP and text files to improve compatibility, especially in incognito mode. Updated manifest with new version, author, and homepage.

- Ensure boolean type for Tor button state checks
  Wrapped `tor_exists` in `bool()` when setting enabled state for test and start Tor buttons to ensure correct type is used. This improves code clarity and prevents potential issues with non-boolean values.

- Update CI to use libasound2t64 on Ubuntu
  Replaces `libasound2` with `libasound2t64` in the list of packages installed on Ubuntu in the CI workflow. This ensures compatibility with updated package naming conventions.

- Update dependencies and Debian system requirements
  Added `types-requests` to test requirements and several new Debian system packages under `system_requires` for better compatibility. Removed `asyncio` from the main requirements list.

- Improve Tor auto-detection and fix image preview loading
  Enhanced Tor executable auto-detection to search app-local directories before system locations, including walking subfolders for tor binaries. Fixed image preview loading by wrapping downloaded data in `QByteArray` for `QPixmap`. Added type stubs for `fake_useragent` and `qtawesome`. Updated tests to cover new Tor detection logic.

- Improve API fetch robustness and manifest compatibility
  Enhances the extension's ability to fetch post data by adding fallback parsing, background fetches with custom headers, and improved error handling for sites with non-standard API responses or authentication requirements. Updates the manifest to use Manifest V2 for cross-browser compatibility and documents MV2/MV3 differences and troubleshooting steps in the README.

## v5.8.0 (07 January 2025)
**feat: Enhanced download capabilities, Tor compatibility, and UI improvements**
- Fix Tor startup issues on Linux and cross-platform compatibility. Create temporary torrc file to avoid system config conflicts on Linux. Use --torc-file argument for clean Tor initialization.
- Add FLAC file support to downloader and preview. This commit adds support for the FLAC audio file format across the creator and post downloader modules. FLAC files can now be detected, previewed, and filtered using the UI checkboxes.
- Add option to download post text as desc.txt. Introduces a checkbox in both creator and post downloaders to enable downloading post text content as desc.txt. Implements logic to fetch, parse, and save post descriptions, with translations and logging for success or failure. Updates language file with new translation keys.
- Enable multi-selection and bulk actions in post/file lists. Updated both CreatorDownloaderTab and PostDownloaderTab to support extended selection in their respective QListWidgets. Checkbox toggling and item highlighting now apply to all selected items, allowing for bulk operations. Refactored selection handling and removed single-item click handlers in favor of selection change events.
- Improve URL parsing and query handling for creator downloads. Enhanced URL parsing logic to robustly extract service and creator IDs, including handling of query parameters such as offset and search queries. Added support for single-page requests and improved error handling for malformed URLs. Updated related methods to consistently clean extracted values and handle unexpected URL structures.

